      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "Martin Scorsese's Shutter Island masterfully blends psychological thriller and neo-noir elements, following U.S. Marshal Teddy Daniels investigating a disappearance at an isolated mental hospital. The film's unreliable narrator approach echoes <a href=\"/movie/77\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"77\">Memento</a> (2000) and <a href=\"/movie/550\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"550\">Fight Club</a> (1999), while its asylum setting draws from classic psychological horror like <a href=\"/movie/510\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"510\">One Flew Over the Cuckoo's Nest</a> (1975). Leonardo DiCaprio's increasingly paranoid performance anchors the film's exploration of trauma, guilt, and self-deception."
      },
