      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "The film's exploration of memory and trauma connects to a broader cinematic tradition including <a href=\"/movie/1903\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"1903\">Vanilla Sky</a> (2001) and Abre Los Ojos (1997). The way Shutter Island handles its unreliable narrator twist differs from similar films like <a href=\"/movie/745\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"745\">The Sixth Sense</a> (1999) by focusing more on emotional truth than narrative surprise. The protagonist's journey through denial and acceptance mirrors elements of <a href=\"/movie/453\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"453\">A Beautiful Mind</a> (2001)."
      }
